IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ta97-connection`

-- Telecommunications Act 1997, Part 19 -- worked cases, from the seat of the person or business wanting a connection.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the deposited text (C2026C00224), never copied from the encoding's output. No scenario life raised this Part; the
-- facts are the encoder's, HYPOTHETICAL throughout. Judgments for the provider or a court are given as facts.
--
-- A breached or still-pending DEONTIC cannot be asserted on the stable l4 (comparing it with EQUALS does not give FALSE), so
-- the regulative rules are asserted where the trace ends FULFILLED and #TRACEd, with an "-- expect:" line, where it does not.
-- Clocks: business days for s 360P and s 360SA, days for s 360VE.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 360A, s 360AA. HYPOTHETICAL: Priya's fibre service, 100/20 Mbps peak: qualifying fixed-line.
#ASSERT `Is it a qualifying carriage service` `a line to the premises (such as fibre, copper or cable)` TRUE 100 20 FALSE FALSE
-- Exactly 25/5 is enough ("at least").
#ASSERT `Is it a qualifying carriage service` `a line to the premises (such as fibre, copper or cable)` TRUE 25 5 FALSE FALSE
-- 25/4 is not.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is it a qualifying carriage service` `a line to the premises (such as fibre, copper or cable)` TRUE 25 4 FALSE FALSE)
-- Satellite at 25/5: yes. A mobile service at 100/20: no (excluded from each definition).
#ASSERT `Is it a qualifying carriage service` `a satellite` TRUE 25 5 FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is it a qualifying carriage service` `a public mobile network` TRUE 100 20 TRUE TRUE)
-- Fixed wireless at 50/10, marketed as fixed wireless and listed: yes; not a listed carriage service: no.
#ASSERT `Is it a qualifying carriage service` `a fixed wireless technology platform` TRUE 50 10 TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is it a qualifying carriage service` `a fixed wireless technology platform` TRUE 50 10 TRUE FALSE)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- ss 360C-360L. Priya's house in an established suburb: NBN Co.
#ASSERT `Who is my statutory infrastructure provider question` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NBN Co: my premises are in the general service area (ss 360F, 360G)`
-- HYPOTHETICAL: Sam buys in a new estate whose network a private carrier installed and declared: that carrier.
#ASSERT `Who is my statutory infrastructure provider question` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the carrier or carriage service provider whose declaration made my nominated service area, unless the Minister has declared another (s 360K)`
-- A designated area overrides a nominated one (s 360H(1)(b)).
#ASSERT `Who is my statutory infrastructure provider question` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the carrier or carriage service provider the Minister declared for my designated service area; where there are several, any of them may meet the obligations (s 360L)`
-- HYPOTHETICAL: Lena's estate is named in an anticipatory notice. Before any home is finished and occupied: a pending area,
-- no provider. Once one is: an anticipated service area, the notice-giver.
#ASSERT `Who is my statutory infrastructure provider question` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `none yet: my premises are in a pending area (an area named in an anticipatory notice where no building unit is yet completed and occupied), which is in no service area (s 360F(1)(aa), (2))`
#ASSERT `Who is my statutory infrastructure provider question` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the carrier or carriage service provider that gave the anticipatory notice for my anticipated service area, unless the Minister has declared another (ss 360KA, 360KB)`
-- Premises in the notice area that NBN Co already serves are not pending (s 360F(2)(c)): NBN Co.
#ASSERT `Who is my statutory infrastructure provider question` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `NBN Co: my premises are in the general service area (ss 360F, 360G)`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 360P(1). Priya, NBN area, her retailer asks, the request is reasonable, fixed-line reasonable: a fixed-line connection.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to be connected question` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the statutory infrastructure provider must connect my premises to a qualifying fixed-line network, so my retailer can supply me fixed-line broadband of at least 25/5 Mbps peak (s 360P(1)(a))`
-- HYPOTHETICAL: Tom's farm, where a fixed-line connection is taken not to be reasonable (s 360P(10)): fixed wireless or satellite.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to be connected question` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: a fixed-line connection is not reasonable, so the statutory infrastructure provider must connect my premises to a network for qualifying fixed wireless or satellite broadband of at least 25/5 Mbps peak (s 360P(1)(b))`
-- Priya rings NBN Co herself; no retailer has asked: not yet.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to be connected question` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not yet: the obligation arises only on a reasonable request by a carriage service provider on my behalf, so I must ask a retailer to make the request (s 360P(1))`
-- An unreasonable request; a Ministerial exclusion; Lena's pending area.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to be connected question` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: the request is not a reasonable request, so no obligation arises (s 360P(1))`
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to be connected question` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: a Ministerial determination under s 360P(3) says no obligation arises in my circumstances (s 360P(2))`
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to be connected question` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: my premises are in a pending area, which is in no service area, so there is no statutory infrastructure provider for them yet (s 360F(2))`
-- Sam, nominated area, request made: fixed-line, from the estate's carrier.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to be connected question` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the statutory infrastructure provider must connect my premises to a qualifying fixed-line network, so my retailer can supply me fixed-line broadband of at least 25/5 Mbps peak (s 360P(1)(a))`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 360P(11A), (12). The provider has 10 business days, or a longer period the Minister specifies (say 15).
#ASSERT `How many business days does the provider have to answer` 0 EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `How many business days does the provider have to answer` 15 EQUALS 15
-- A shorter "longer period" is not one: still 10.
#ASSERT `How many business days does the provider have to answer` 7 EQUALS 10
-- Refused: 5 business days to give reasons, 5 more after the retailer receives them. Received the same day: 10; 2 days later: 12.
#ASSERT `How long until I must have the refusal reasons` 0 EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `How long until I must have the refusal reasons` 2 EQUALS 12

-- The duty chain for Priya, with a 20-business-day maximum connection period in NBN Co's published terms (an input).
-- The provider says yes on day 4 and connects on day 18: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 360P(1), (11A), (12) -- the provider must answer my retailer's request, connect me or give reasons, and my retailer must pass the reasons on` 0 20) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the statutory infrastructure provider` (`answer the request` `will fulfil the request`) 4), (EVENT `the statutory infrastructure provider` `connect my premises` 18)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Refused on day 9, reasons on day 14, the retailer passes them to Priya on day 19: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 360P(1), (11A), (12) -- the provider must answer my retailer's request, connect me or give reasons, and my retailer must pass the reasons on` 0 20) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the statutory infrastructure provider` (`answer the request` `refuses the request`) 9), (EVENT `the statutory infrastructure provider` `give my carriage service provider written notice of the refusal and the reasons` 14), (EVENT `my carriage service provider` `give me a copy of the refusal notice` 19)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the statutory infrastructure provider, "s 360P(11A): ..." (no answer by day 10)
#TRACE `s 360P(1), (11A), (12) -- the provider must answer my retailer's request, connect me or give reasons, and my retailer must pass the reasons on` 0 20 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 11)
-- expect: BREACH BY the statutory infrastructure provider, "s 360P(12)(c): ..." (refused on day 9, reasons only on day 15)
#TRACE `s 360P(1), (11A), (12) -- the provider must answer my retailer's request, connect me or give reasons, and my retailer must pass the reasons on` 0 20 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the statutory infrastructure provider` DOES `answer the request` `refuses the request` AT 9
    PARTY `the statutory infrastructure provider` DOES `give my carriage service provider written notice of the refusal and the reasons` AT 15
-- expect: BREACH BY my carriage service provider, "s 360P(12)(d): ..." (reasons received day 14, passed on only on day 20)
#TRACE `s 360P(1), (11A), (12) -- the provider must answer my retailer's request, connect me or give reasons, and my retailer must pass the reasons on` 0 20 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the statutory infrastructure provider` DOES `answer the request` `refuses the request` AT 9
    PARTY `the statutory infrastructure provider` DOES `give my carriage service provider written notice of the refusal and the reasons` AT 14
    PARTY `my carriage service provider` DOES `give me a copy of the refusal notice` AT 20
-- expect: BREACH BY the statutory infrastructure provider, "s 360P(1), (9), s 360W(2): ..." (yes on day 4, not connected by day 24)
#TRACE `s 360P(1), (11A), (12) -- the provider must answer my retailer's request, connect me or give reasons, and my retailer must pass the reasons on` 0 20 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the statutory infrastructure provider` DOES `answer the request` `will fulfil the request` AT 4
    (WAITUNTIL 25)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 360P(8), (9). No agreement: the website terms at the time of the request. An agreement: its terms. Asked for one on
-- the published terms: the provider must enter it.
#ASSERT `On what terms question` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the terms the provider published on its website when the request was made, including the maximum connection period, except where they are inconsistent with a standard or rules (ss 360P(9), 360W(2), (4))`
#ASSERT `On what terms question` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the terms of the agreement between the provider and my retailer that covers the connection`
#ASSERT `On what terms question` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `an agreement on the published terms: my retailer asked for one, and the provider must enter it (s 360P(8))`

-- s 360Q(1A), (1B). Priya's fibre: voice calls required. Tom's satellite: not.
#ASSERT `Must the wholesale service support voice calls` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the wholesale service support voice calls` TRUE)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- ss 360R, 360SA. Sam's estate carrier gives notice it will stop being able to serve the estate; his retailer receives it
-- and his service is likely to be disrupted: told within 5 business days. NBN Co in the general service area: no Part 19
-- notice. Not likely to affect his service: no s 360SA notice. Not yet received: not yet.
#ASSERT `Must I be told question` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: my retailer must give me written notice of the matter within 5 business days after it receives the provider's notice (s 360SA)`
#ASSERT `Must I be told question` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no notice under Part 19: s 360R does not apply to NBN Co as the provider for the general service area`
#ASSERT `Must I be told question` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no notice under s 360SA: it applies only where the matter is likely to change or disrupt the qualifying services my retailer provides me`
#ASSERT `Must I be told question` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not yet: my retailer must tell me within 5 business days of receiving a notice under s 360R(2) or (3), and has not received one`
-- The retailer's duty, clock from receipt: told on day 5, fulfilled; nothing by day 6, breached.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `s 360SA(2) -- my retailer must tell me of the provider's notice within 5 business days` 0 (LIST (EVENT `my carriage service provider` `give me written notice of the matter` 5)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY my carriage service provider, "s 360SA(2): ..."
#TRACE `s 360SA(2) -- my retailer must tell me of the provider's notice within 5 business days` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 6)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 360VD. HYPOTHETICAL: the compensation rules give Priya $300 for a missed connection date; NBN Co already credited her
-- $120 for the same event under her retailer's terms: $180. Credited $400: nil, not below zero.
#ASSERT `Can I claim damages question` TRUE TRUE 300 120 EQUALS `yes: the provider is liable to pay me damages for the contravention, in the amount the compensation rules give less what I have already been credited or paid for the same event (s 360VD)` 180
#ASSERT `Can I claim damages question` TRUE TRUE 300 400 EQUALS `yes: the provider is liable to pay me damages for the contravention, in the amount the compensation rules give less what I have already been credited or paid for the same event (s 360VD)` 0
#ASSERT `Can I claim damages question` FALSE TRUE 300 0 EQUALS `no: s 360VD gives damages only for a contravention of a designated compensable standard or rule that relates to me as the provider's customer or prospective customer`
-- s 360VD(7): a contravention on 3 March 2026: sue by 3 March 2028. One beginning 29 February 2028: by 28 February 2030.
#ASSERT `By when must I sue for damages` (Date 3 3 2026) EQUALS Date 3 3 2028
#ASSERT `By when must I sue for damages` (Date 29 2 2028) EQUALS Date 28 2 2030

-- s 360VE. 14 days to decide, then 14 weeks (98 days): 112 days at most; with 30 relevant days declared, 128.
#ASSERT `How many days until the provider must pay or refuse` 0 EQUALS 112
#ASSERT `How many days until the provider must pay or refuse` 30 EQUALS 128
-- Accepts on day 10, credits on day 100 (within 98 of day 10): fulfilled. Refuses on day 14, notifies on day 112: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 360VE -- the provider must decide on liability, then pay me or tell me it will not` 0) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the statutory infrastructure provider` (`decide whether to accept liability for damages` `accepts the liability`) 10), (EVENT `the statutory infrastructure provider` `discharge the liability` 100)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 360VE -- the provider must decide on liability, then pay me or tell me it will not` 0) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the statutory infrastructure provider` (`decide whether to accept liability for damages` `does not accept the liability`) 14), (EVENT `the statutory infrastructure provider` `give me written notification that it does not accept liability` 112)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the statutory infrastructure provider, "s 360VE(4), (5): ..." (accepted day 10, paid day 109)
#TRACE `s 360VE -- the provider must decide on liability, then pay me or tell me it will not` 0 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the statutory infrastructure provider` DOES `decide whether to accept liability for damages` `accepts the liability` AT 10
    PARTY `the statutory infrastructure provider` DOES `discharge the liability` AT 109
-- expect: BREACH BY the statutory infrastructure provider, "s 360VE(1): ..." (no decision by day 14)
#TRACE `s 360VE -- the provider must decide on liability, then pay me or tell me it will not` 0 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 15)
